            "review_title": "Review at Man Tu Vegan",
            "review_text": "PFG\nSydney, Australia105 contributions\n0\nThe best buffet in Ho Chi Minh! Pay by donation so please, travellers, be generous\nJun 2019 • Solo\nI found this place by accident walking back from Saigon Centre. Its a little hole in the wall in the alley between two old buildings. They serve dinner from 6pm and absolutely EVERYTHING is vegan! Even non vegans will be amazed at the wide variety of appetizers, mains, soups, fake meat and desserts!\nI have been five times in five days and absolutely love the freshness of the salads, soups with little to no oil, stir frys (about five to choose from) and about ten varieties of tofu. Im pretty sure its a not for profit so please donate at least $50,000 VND per person which is just over $2 USD. \nEveryone is very lovely although no english is spoken. The decor is beautiful full of buddhas, lotus flowers, mandalas and very well kept in terms of cleanliness and tidyness.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 5, 2019",
